`<Select.List>` allows parts like `<Select.Arrow>` and `<Select.ScrollArrow>` to escape the `overflow: scroll` context

https://deploy-preview-2596--base-ui.netlify.app/experiments/long-select

Fixes #2516
Fixes #2046

## Breaking changes

It is now possible for `Select.ScrollArrow` to show when in fallback (`alignItemWithTrigger` deactivated). As a result, the styles should be updated like so to match before:

```css
.ScrollArrow {
  display: none; /* instead of display: flex */

  &[data-side="none"] { 
    display: flex;
  }
}
```

Otherwise, the demos have been updated to use `Select.List`, where the scroll arrows are also visible in fallback mode. If you're using `alignItemWithTrigger={false}` and don't want scroll arrows, you can omit `Select.List` (unless using `Select.Arrow`, which is rare) and `Select.ScrollArrow`s from the JSX entirely.
